## Statement

Compute $\displaystyle\lim_{x\to0}\frac{e^x-1-x}{x^2}$.

## Hint

Use the Taylor expansion of $e^x$ at $0$ up to order $2$.

## Solution

As $x\to0$, $e^x=1+x+\dfrac{x^2}{2}+o(x^2)$.

Therefore $\dfrac{e^x-1-x}{x^2}=\dfrac12+o(1)$, and the limit is $\dfrac12$.
